      "why": "pipelined is the only family with feasible designs (30/53) and owns the entire merged front; it is the only family that can meet the 32 Msps throughput constraint (1 result/cycle). The current best feasible area is 39385 um^2. I am narrowing the ranges to focus the remaining budget on the region of the front that is actually feasible: data_width 14-16 (14 is the minimum that can plausibly give 12+ bits accuracy with enough n_iter; 16 gives margin), n_iter 12-16 (12 is near the minimum for 12-bit accuracy; higher n_iter increases area without much accuracy gain once past ~14), angle_guard -2 to 2 (negative guards save area but risk accuracy; positive guards add area), frac_guard 0-2 (0 is cheapest; higher guards add area for marginal accuracy), and both rounding modes. This tightens the search around the known feasible region to map the Pareto front more densely within the remaining budget."
