  "rationale": "The fleet facts are decisive: only pipelined has produced feasible designs (30/53) and it owns all 7 designs on the merged front. iterative, unrolled_k, and pipelined_m have 0 feasible designs. The throughput constraint (>= 32 Msps) requires 1 result/cycle, which only pipelined and pipelined_m can provide; pipelined_m has failed to find any feasible design in 47 evaluations, likely because the register-every-m-stages structure either cannot meet the accuracy constraint at low area or the Fmax drops too much. I am therefore concentrating all remaining budget on pipelined with tightly narrowed ranges around the known feasible region (data_width 14-16, n_iter 12-16, angle_guard -2 to 2, frac_guard 0-2). The goal is to densely map the Pareto front in the area-vs-accuracy trade-off space within the feasible region, since the selection rule is min area and the hypervolume rewards covering the trade-off curve. The current best feasible area is 39385 um^2; I expect to find designs with lower area by exploring the boundary of the accuracy constraint (data_width=14, n_iter=12-14, angle_guard=-2, frac_guard=0) while also mapping the higher-accuracy corner (data_width=16, n_iter=14-16) for hypervolume coverage. I am not including pipelined_m because it has 0 feasible designs in 47 evaluations and the remaining budget is better spent densifying the pipelined front."
